# Squares with three loaded edges: the runs of the thirteen-face theorem

Generated by `ai_research_notes/outerplanar/t4b_m0/emit_sqmulti.py runs`. For each run of
`ai_research_notes/OUTERPLANAR_13_15_LEAN_PLAN.md` §2.2 (the "7" of the thirteen-face note
`ai_research_notes/OUTERPLANAR_THIRTEEN_AND_GAUGE_OBSTRUCTION_2026-11-23.md`, Lemma 1, and the
two-distinguished, `three_heavy` and `four_heavy` laws of
`ai_research_notes/outerplanar/square_two_heavy.py`): the property of the 52 patterns of the
cover, from the 52 records of `Outerplanar/SqMultiData/`, and the list-level theorem. In each,
`W j` is the profile of the path edge `j` of a square `u x₀ x₁ v` (lists `Lu`, `Li 0`, `Li 1`,
`Lv`), and `N j` its scale.

The certificates are exact (kernel-checked integer Gibbs inequalities, no logarithms); they
replace the float-oracle certificates of `cert_square_H_exact.py` and `square_two_heavy.py`,
which were re-solved for this format on the 52 saturated patterns instead of the 4202 list
configurations.
-/

namespace Outerplanar.SqMulti

open Finset

theorem sqClass_zero {S T : Finset ℕ} {W : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ} {N : ℝ} :
    sqClass 0 S T W N = InBall S T W N := by simp [sqClass]

theorem sqClass_one {S T : Finset ℕ} {W : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ} {N : ℝ} :
    sqClass 1 S T W N = BijGe S T W N 1 := by simp [sqClass]

theorem sqClass_two {S T : Finset ℕ} {W : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ} {N : ℝ} :
    sqClass 2 S T W N = Hex S T W N := by simp [sqClass]

